1. Introduction

The Student Record System is a Java-based application developed to manage student information efficiently. It allows users to add, search, update, delete, and display student records. The project applies Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts to create a well-structured and maintainable system.

2. Problem Statement

Managing student records manually is time-consuming and can lead to errors such as lost files, duplicate records, and inaccurate information. Educational institutions need a computerized system that stores and manages student records efficiently.

3. Objectives
General Objective

To develop a Student Record System using Java and Object-Oriented Programming principles.

Specific Objectives
Add new student records.
Search for students using their ID.
Update student information.
Delete student records.
Display all stored student records.
Practice and demonstrate Java OOP concepts.
4. Scope of the Project

The Student Record System performs the following tasks:

Register new students.
Store student information.
Search student records.
Update existing records.
Delete student records.
Display all student records.

The project is designed as a console-based Java application.

