8. System Design

The application is divided into different classes, each responsible for a specific task.

Main Class

Displays the menu and controls program execution.

Student Class

Represents a student object and stores student information.

StudentManager Class

Performs operations such as adding, searching, updating, deleting, and displaying student records.

9. Object-Oriented Programming Concepts Used
Encapsulation

Student data is stored in private variables and accessed using getter and setter methods.

Inheritance

Inheritance allows one class to inherit properties and methods from another class if implemented.

Polymorphism

Polymorphism enables methods to perform different tasks through method overloading or overriding.

Abstraction

Complex operations are hidden inside methods, making the system easier to understand and maintain.

